{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "כברכת", :translit "k'virkhat", :gloss "like the blessing of"} {:he "כברכת ה' אלהיך אשר נתן לך", :translit "k'virkhat Hashem Elokekha asher natan lakh", :gloss "like the blessing of YHWH your God that He has given you"} {:he "עולת ראיה", :translit "olat re'iyah", :gloss "burnt offering of appearance"} {:he "מי שיש לו אוכלין מרובין מביא עולות מרובים", :translit "mi she'yesh lo okhlin merubin meivi olot merubim", :gloss "one who has abundant food brings abundant burnt offerings"} {:he "תזבח ואכלת בשר", :translit "tizbach v'akhalta basar", :gloss "you shall slaughter and eat flesh"} {:he "תזבח", :translit "tizbach", :gloss "you shall slaughter"} {:he "עולה", :translit "olah", :gloss "burnt offering"} {:he "ואכלת בשר", :translit "v'akhalta basar", :gloss "and eat flesh"} {:he "שלמים", :translit "shelamim", :gloss "peace offerings"} {:he "ברכת ה' אלהיך אשר נתן לך", :translit "birkhat Hashem Elokekha asher natan lakh", :gloss "the blessing of YHWH your God that He has given you"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "The letter כ ('like') links our verse's phrase to the identical wording in Deuteronomy 12:6, establishing that the scale of slaughter here mirrors the scale of the pilgrimage offerings there."}], :frame {:text "Mishnah Hagigah 1:2 states that one who has abundant food brings abundant olot. The verse 'you shall slaughter and eat flesh' is read as a single sequence: 'you shall slaughter' corresponds to the olah (wholly consumed on the altar), while 'and eat flesh' corresponds to shelamim (partially eaten by the offerer). Both offering categories thus multiply in proportion to God's blessing, echoing the phrase 'the blessing of YHWH your God that He has given you' which appears in Deuteronomy 12:6–7 in the context of olot and shelamim.", :sources ["Mishnah Hagigah 1:2" "Deuteronomy 12:6" "Deuteronomy 12:7"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "The letter כ ('like') links our verse's phrase to the identical wording in Deuteronomy 12:6, establishing that the scale of slaughter here mirrors the scale of the pilgrimage offerings there.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:36:15.442748308Z", :model "glm-5.2"}